I walk up to the checkout.
I have the basket in my hand.
I put the food on the belt.
First I take the rye bread from the basket.
Then I take the milk and the parsnip.
I also take carrots and black beans.
Finally I put the pastry on the belt.
The cashier sits behind the checkout.
He smiles at me.
"Hello," he says.
"Hello," I reply.
He scans the food quickly.
I take my card out.
I hold the card over the machine.
The machine beeps.
"Would you like to have the receipt?" he asks.
"Yes please, I would like to have the receipt," I say.
I open my bag.
I pack the bag quickly.
"Have a good day," he says.
